{"title":"Cuboid","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Cuboid&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p>A <b>cuboid</b> is a solid that has six rectangular faces--think of a typical box. All faces are either <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> to each other. Further, a <b>cuboid</b> is a right rectangular <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prism\" title=\"Prism\">prism</a>. A <b>cuboid</b> with six square faces is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube\" title=\"Cube\">cube</a>, whereas a <b>cuboid</b> with at least two square faces is known as a <b>square cuboid</b>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finding_Area_and_Volume_of_a_Cuboid\">Finding Area and Volume of a Cuboid</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cuboid&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Finding Area and Volume of a Cuboid\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a given cuboid has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3d9b424fcffe6d4482e03cc0c43c3e601fb37a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\times b \\times c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />, then its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e077c21f27f6c822ae8db4db736776895ccfe8ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot b \\cdot c$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, and its surface area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b364c0a540e09ae8fbbdb9a1fce4adcd2efe49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ab + 2bc + 2ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finding_the_space_diagonal_of_a_cuboid\">Finding the space diagonal of a cuboid</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cuboid&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Finding the space diagonal of a cuboid\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The space diagonal of a cuboid, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, is found by the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/35747ba51abcf670e6803e309c1e65d19557a036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d^2=a^2+b^2+c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the side lengths of the solid\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cuboid&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube\" title=\"Cube\">Cube</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelepiped\" title=\"Parallelepiped\">Parallelepiped</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">Parallelogram</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081846\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 61/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1403/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.178      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.178      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5068:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081846 and revision id 78337. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}